        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "2979eddb-fb81-5f02-acdc-8afaef984c1c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Minardi M190, Minardi M189B, Cosworth DFR V8 engine, Pirelli tyres\n- Companies: Pirelli & C. S.p.A., ChemChina, Pirelli North America, Bohn Aluminum, Wicks\n- People: James Edward Arnold\n- Places: Milan, Italy\n\nFacts:\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. has been based in Milan, Italy, and it was formerly listed on the Milan Stock Exchange starting in 1922.\n- Pirelli & C. S.p.A. is now an overseas subsidiary of the Chinese state-owned enterprise ChemChina.\n- The Minardi M189 was updated as the Minardi M189B for the season, and the Minardi M189B was used for the first two races of the year before the Minardi M190 replaced it.\n- The Minardi M190 was powered by the Cosworth DFR V8 engine and ran on Pirelli tyres.\n- James Edward Arnold was one of the last presidents of Pirelli North America, and he was also president of Bohn Aluminum and a major consultant to Wicks, the group known for owning the Lowe's hardware chain.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
